Yes — sudden weather changes including snow are very common at **Laguna Los Patos in Torres del Paine National Park** (Chilean Patagonia). A hiker on the W‑trek in late April described being at the lake when “snowflakes swirled around us” and moments later “an icy wind blew raindrops against our cheeks, so hard that it stung,” noting the local warning that you can experience “4 seasons in one day” in Torres del Paine [Chilling in Chile](w1). The region’s exposed, high‑latitude setting means conditions can shift from sun to snow, rain, and fierce wind within minutes, even in summer.

If you’re planning to visit, pack full waterproof/windproof layers, warm insulation, and be prepared for rapid changes at any time of year.

